  "limitations": [
    "The task of rendering is made complex by factors that affect thermal perception, including poor spatial resolution, spatial summation, high thresholds, and slow rates of thermal change.",
    "Most friction models are not consistent with the Coulomb model, leading to different simulation results and performance strongly dependent on defined velocity thresholds (which lack physical interpretation).",
    "Haptic rendering of deformable bodies poses major challenges, as sufficiently realistic implementations suitable for real-time simulation of anisotropic, inhomogeneous, and nonlinear material properties must be found.",
    "Finite element (FE) models are computationally very expensive and consequently are often used only for offline simulation rather than in real time.",
    "The methods for the haptic rendering of deformable bodies tend to take a procedural approach that neglects critical factors related to human exploration, for example, thresholds or effects of dynamic haptic perception."
  ],
